      "id": 14,
      "options": {
        "content": "# Scrapy Web Scraping & PostgresML Machine Learning Dashboard\n\n## Service Information\n\n### Scrapy Configuration\n- **Location**: `/home/dev/Scrapy/`\n- **Containers**: Scrapyd (6800) + Scrapyd-UI (3007)\n- **Default Project**: searchbot\n- **Web Interface**: http://localhost:3007 (when running)\n- **API Endpoint**: http://localhost:6800\n\n### PostgresML Configuration\n- **Location**: Docker Container (ghcr.io/postgresml/postgresml:2.9.3)\n- **Database Port**: 5433 (localhost:5433)\n- **Dashboard Port**: 8100 (http://localhost:8100)\n- **User**: postgres\n- **Status**: Running ✅\n\n## Usage Examples\n\n### Scrapy Commands\n```bash\n# Start Scrapy\ncd /home/dev/Scrapy && docker-compose up -d\n\n# Check status\ndocker-compose ps\n\n# View logs\ndocker-compose logs -f\n\n# Stop Scrapy\ndocker-compose down\n```\n\n### PostgresML Commands\n```bash\n# Connect to database\npsql -h localhost -p 5433 -U postgres\n\n# Access dashboard\nhttp://localhost:8100\n\n# Train a model\nSELECT * FROM pgml.train('model_name', 'classification', 'table_name', 'target_column');\n\n# Make predictions\nSELECT pgml.predict('model_name', ARRAY[...]);\n```\n\n## Integration Points\n- Both services integrate with n8n (workflow automation)\n- PostgresML can store Scrapy results\n- Redis (port 6379) available for both\n- Ollama (port 11434) available for ML features\n\n## Documentation\n- Scrapy Details: `/home/dev/SCRAPY_SERVICE_DETAILS.md`\n- PostgresML Details: `/home/dev/POSTGRESML_SERVICE_DETAILS.md`\n- Infrastructure: `/home/dev/INFRASTRUCTURE_SUMMARY.md`",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "8.0.0",
      "title": "Documentation & Quick Links",
      "type": "text"
    }
